    "prose": "Rain drummed harder over the covered yard, and wind sent a cold spray across the edge of the sheltered route. Aya and Mert still held the restored mosaic between them, each supporting one side.\n\nThe level covered ramp stretched toward the open gallery door. Aya looked along it and felt the urge to hurry. Then Mert adjusted his next step, and the panel shifted by the smallest amount between their hands.\n\n“Can we go slower?” Aya asked. “I want us to keep the panel level.”\n\nMert looked directly at her. He had heard the request, and his serious nod showed that he understood.\n\n“Slower,” he agreed.\n\nHe shortened his next step and waited before taking another. His pace settled into a careful rhythm for their shared carry.\n\nAya watched him make the change. Only when she was certain she could follow that rhythm did she move.\n\nAya crossed the level covered ramp from the covered yard to the gallery entry. She kept her side from rising or pulling ahead.\n\nMert crossed the level covered ramp from the covered yard to the gallery entry. He matched the slower shared pace all the way.\n\nThe same fragile mosaic panel crossed the level covered ramp from the covered yard to the gallery entry between them. It remained level, restored, and intact in their two-person hold.\n\nAt the entry, they stopped together. The wide gallery door stood open ahead, but they did not pass through it.\n\nAya breathed out carefully. “That was better.”\n\nMert glanced at the panel, then back at her. “Better than rushing.”\n\nRain rattled behind them. Aya did not argue.",
